# DYD 2026 on iPhone — PWA + GitHub Pages (free hosting, offline)

Apple does not let you sideload a Flutter **.ipa** without a Mac, Xcode, and a paid
Developer account. The practical route for iPhone is a **Progressive Web App (PWA)**:
build the same Flutter project for **web**, host it on **GitHub Pages** (HTTPS + free),
then **Add to Home Screen** in Safari so it behaves like an installed app and works
**offline** after the first load.

Live site (after deploy):

**https://kreativkento.github.io/dyd2026/**

---

## How it works (short)

| Piece | Role |
|--------|------|
| `flutter build web` | Compiles your app + bundles JSON/images |
| `manifest.json` + icons | “Installable” app name, colors, home-screen icon |
| Flutter service worker | Caches the app shell and assets for offline use |
| GitHub Pages | Free HTTPS hosting (required for PWA on iPhone) |
| Safari → Add to Home Screen | Full-screen icon on the iPhone home screen |

---

## Part 1 — One-time GitHub setup

1. Push this repo to **https://github.com/kreativkento/dyd2026** (already configured as `origin`).
2. On GitHub: **Settings → Pages → Build and deployment**
   - **Source:** **GitHub Actions** (not “Deploy from branch”).
3. Ensure the default branch is **`main`** or **`master`** (the workflow listens to both).

The workflow file is already in the repo:

`.github/workflows/deploy-pages.yml`

It runs on every push to `main`/`master`, builds the PWA with `--base-href "/dyd2026/"`, and publishes `build/web`.

