## Part 3 — Build the PWA locally (optional, before push)

Same build the CI runs:

```powershell
cd "C:\Users\Kent Veloso\Desktop\DEV PROJECTS\dyd2026"
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\scripts\build_web.ps1
```

Output folder: **`build\web`**

- **`--base-href "/dyd2026/"`** matches GitHub Pages (repo name as subpath).
- **`404.html`** is copied from **`index.html`** so deep links and refresh work on Pages.

Test on your Wi‑Fi network before deploying:

```powershell
# Local-only base path (easier to serve)
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\scripts\build_web.ps1 -BaseHref "/"
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\scripts\serve_web.ps1
```

On iPhone (same Wi‑Fi): Safari → `http://<your-pc-ip>:8080`

